<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;'>Note: Choose the correct answer from the given options.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> What is the return type specified for a constructor in Java?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) int</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) void</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Same as the class name</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Constructors do not have any return type, not even void</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Which of the following statements is TRUE regarding constructors in Java?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) A constructor can be declared as static.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) A constructor must have the exact same name as the class.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) A constructor is called using explicit method invocation.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) A constructor is executed only when a class is imported.</li></ul>
